---
import Article from '../../components/Article.astro';

const title = 'The Best Free Solitaire & Puzzle Games to Play Online | CardHearth';
const description =
  'A friendly tour of the best free solitaire and puzzle games you can play in your browser — Klondike, Spider, FreeCell, Sudoku, Mahjong, Minesweeper, 2048 and more. No download, no sign-up.';
const updated = '2026-06-13';
const heading = 'The Best Free Solitaire & Puzzle Games';
const subtitle =
  'Every game on CardHearth is free, runs in your browser, and needs no sign-up. Here is which one to play depending on your mood.';

const breadcrumb = [
  { name: 'CardHearth', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' },
  { name: 'Best Free Solitaire & Puzzle Games', href: '/guides/best-free-solitaire-and-puzzle-games/' },
];

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'The Best Free Solitaire & Puzzle Games to Play Online',
    description,
    datePublished: updated,
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Person', '@id': 'https://cardhearth.com/#jared', name: 'Jared Waterworth', url: 'https://cardhearth.com/about/' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'CardHearth',
      url: 'https://cardhearth.com/',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://cardhearth.com/logo.png', width: 512, height: 512 },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: 'https://cardhearth.com/guides/best-free-solitaire-and-puzzle-games/',
    image: 'https://cardhearth.com/og.png',
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: breadcrumb.map((c, i) => ({
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: i + 1,
      name: c.name,
      item: `https://cardhearth.com${c.href}`,
    })),
  },
];
---

<Article
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading={heading}
  subtitle={subtitle}
  updated={updated}
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumb={breadcrumb}
  cta={{ href: '/', label: 'Browse all games' }}
>
  <p>
    There are a lot of places to play classic games online, and most of them feel a decade old —
    slow pages, cluttered screens, pop-ups everywhere. CardHearth is the opposite: every game
    loads instantly, plays beautifully with a mouse or a finger, and is genuinely free with no
    account required. Below is a quick tour of the whole library so you can pick the right game
    for the moment.
  </p>

  <h2>Solitaire (card games)</h2>

  <h3><a href="/klondike/">Klondike Solitaire</a></h3>
  <p>
    The one most people mean by "Solitaire." Move every card to the foundations, building
    alternating-colour runs along the way. Forgiving, endlessly replayable, and the best place to
    start. New to it? Read <a href="/guides/how-to-win-klondike-solitaire/">how to win Klondike</a>.
  </p>

  <h3><a href="/spider/">Spider Solitaire</a></h3>
  <p>
    Build same-suit runs from King down to Ace across ten columns. The 2-suit game is a great
    middle challenge; 4-suit is for experts. Our <a href="/guides/spider-solitaire-strategy/">Spider
    strategy guide</a> shows how to keep columns open and avoid tangles.
  </p>

  <h3><a href="/freecell/">FreeCell</a></h3>
  <p>
    Every card is on the table from the start, so it's pure planning — and almost every deal is
    winnable. If you like a puzzle you can actually solve with thought rather than luck, this is
    your game. See the <a href="/guides/freecell-strategy/">FreeCell strategy guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Quick rounds: <a href="/pyramid/">Pyramid</a>, <a href="/tripeaks/">TriPeaks</a> &amp; <a href="/golf/">Golf</a></h3>
  <p>
    Three lighter solitaires for a short break. Pyramid has you pairing cards that sum to
    thirteen; TriPeaks rewards long streaks as you clear three peaks; Golf is a fast "play up or
    down" race to empty the course. Perfect for a few minutes between tasks.
  </p>

  <h2>Puzzles</h2>

  <h3><a href="/sudoku/">Sudoku</a></h3>
  <p>
    Pure logic across four difficulties, with pencil marks built in. Every CardHearth puzzle is
    guaranteed solvable without guessing. Learn the full ladder of methods in our
    <a href="/guides/sudoku-solving-techniques/">Sudoku techniques guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h3><a href="/mahjong/">Mahjong Solitaire</a></h3>
  <p>
    Match free pairs of tiles to dismantle the layout. Every CardHearth deal is built to be
    solvable, so a stuck board is a puzzle to read — not a dead end you were handed.
  </p>

  <h3><a href="/minesweeper/">Minesweeper</a> &amp; <a href="/2048/">2048</a></h3>
  <p>
    Two modern classics. Minesweeper is a game of deduction — read the numbers, flag the mines,
    and (on CardHearth) take back a misclick with undo. 2048 is the addictive slide-and-merge
    tile chase. Both are one click away, free.
  </p>

  <h2>A new game every day</h2>
  <p>
    Want variety without choosing? The <a href="/daily-challenge/">Daily Challenge</a> serves one
    hand-picked game each day — the same for everyone — and tracks your streak. It's the easiest
    way to keep a daily habit and discover games you might not have tried.
  </p>

  <h2>Why play on CardHearth</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free, with no sign-up</strong> and nothing to install.</li>
    <li><strong>Fast and clean</strong> — no clutter, works the same on phone and desktop.</li>
    <li><strong>Generous features</strong> — unlimited undo, hints, statistics, streaks, themes,
      and numbered deals you can replay or share with a friend.</li>
    <li><strong>Your progress stays on your device</strong> unless you choose otherwise.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Pick something above, or just <a href="/">browse the full menu</a> and start playing. For
    strategy on the bigger games, the <a href="/guides/">guides hub</a> has you covered.
  </p>
</Article>
